// D10 — Rogue privileged account creation and group addition
// Author:  Jenna Frank (Hot Pink Huntress)
// Hunt:    Hunt 22 "Harborlight" — Akira ransomware, Microsoft Sentinel
// ATT&CK:  T1136.002 (Create Account: Domain Account)
// Source:  Security 4720 / 4728 / 4732; Sysmon EventID 1 (Process Create)
// Status:  Validated by replay against the hunt dataset (2026-10-14). The report
//          Section 13 predates this replay and lists all rules as proposed.
//          Production tuning pending.
//
// Audit events (4720/4728/4732) confirm; the command line is the lead. A lookup
// (net user <name> /domain with no /add) is NOT a creation and must not fire.

HarborlightDental_CL
| where EventTime > ago(1d)
| where EventCode in (4720, 4728, 4732)
     or (EventID == 1 and (
            (CommandLine has_any ("net user", "net localgroup Administrators") and CommandLine has "/add")
            or CommandLine has "Add-ADGroupMember"))
| project EventTime, host, EventCode, EventID, CommandLine

// VALIDATION (ADDC01, 2026-02-04 05:20:00–05:25:00). Confirmed result:
//   05:21:56  net user svc_sql Summer2024! /add /domain   + Security 4720 (created)
//   05:22:28  net localgroup Administrators svc_sql /add   + Security 4732
//   05:22:54  Add-ADGroupMember 'Domain Admins' svc_sql  -> 05:22:57 Security 4728
//   akira_svc decoy lookup (no /add, no 4720) correctly NOT matched.
//
// FP/tuning: legitimate provisioning also creates accounts. Allowlist approved
// provisioning identities/hosts and MSP admin accounts; prioritize additions to
// Domain Admins / Administrators over plain account creation.
